; `mentatd install` hands a unit file to the user's service manager, so only
; its no-touch surfaces run here: --print renders without writing anything,
; and the refusal paths fire before any launchctl/systemctl call — a cram
; must never load a real service. The rendered unit and its path are the
; platform's, so the bodies are split per platform and gated by %{system},
; the sibling sandbox-enforce mechanism: the parent whole-subtree stanza
; attaches every .t here ungated, and each scoped stanza below ANDs in its
; %{system} guard.

(cram
 (applies_to install-macos)
 (alias blackbox)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{system} macosx)))

(cram
 (applies_to install-linux)
 (alias blackbox)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{system} linux)))
